From: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dix: no motion history

The server keeps the last 256 pointer positions of each device for
GetMotionEvents, which no client here asks for: for the virtual core
pointer, 256 entries of three values for each of 36 valuators and a
time, 109 KB calloc'd and never written while nobody reads it.  With an
MMU the untouched pages cost nothing; without one they are RAM.  A history
of 0 allocates none; the connection setup then reports a motion buffer of
size 0, as the core protocol allows, and GetMotionEvents returns no events.

Signed-off-by: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Upstream: N/A sized for a machine without an MMU
---
 dix/getevents.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/dix/getevents.c
+++ b/dix/getevents.c
@@ -71,7 +71,7 @@
 #include "probes.h"
 
 /* Number of motion history events to store. */
-#define MOTION_HISTORY_SIZE 256
+#define MOTION_HISTORY_SIZE 0
 
 /**
  * InputEventList is the storage for input events generated by
